{"name":"Castor oil on brows/lashes","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":26,"casual":{"lead":["Castor oil is a thick plant oil pressed from castor beans, made mostly of triglycerides with ricinoleic acid as the main fatty acid. People brush it onto brows and lashes as a folk remedy for thicker, longer hair, and it is popular online.","Forum users report both positive and underwhelming results. Proponents attribute effects to ricinoleic acid and the oil's conditioning; no clinical study of the practice on brows or lashes was identified."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["A small amount is brushed onto the brows or the lash base, often at night with a clean spoolie or applicator, over weeks. It is commonly used alongside other brow and lash routines."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Topical use is generally described as low risk, but eye-area products can irritate, and the oil should be kept out of the eyes."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Outcomes of posterior lamellar tarsal rotation vs bilamellar tarsal rotation for trachomatous trichiasis.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40737343/","source":"PLoS neglected tropical diseases","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Clinical Trial, Phase III"},{"title":"Double-Blind Comparison of Eyelash Epilation Techniques for the Purpose of Demodex folliculorum Mite Retrieval.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38345025/","source":"Eye & contact lens","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Lotilaner Ophthalmic Solution 0.25% for Demodex Blepharitis: Randomized, Vehicle-Controlled, Multicenter, Phase 3 Trial (Saturn-2).","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37285925/","source":"Ophthalmology","year":2023,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Introduction to Hair Development.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29797270/","source":"Advances in experimental medicine and biology","year":2018,"cites":null,"kin